            <ArticleTitle>[The window in the falciform ligament. A rare case of hernia of the small intestine through the falciform ligament].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>466-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The most common causes for small-bowel obstructions with subsequent strangulation are intra-abdominal adhesions and external hernias. We report an unusual case of strangulated small-bowel hernia through a congenital window in the falciform ligament. The diagnosis and surgical treatment are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
